Title: Social Cohesion, Institutions, and Growth
Abstract: We present evidence that measures of “social cohesion,” such as income inequality
and ethnic fractionalization, endogenously determine institutional quality, which in
turn casually determines growth.
Length: 34 pages
Creation-Date: 2006-08
